The Rotterdam Film Festival ( IFFR ) has hired Pepijn Kuyper as its new Managing Director.

Kuyper succeeds Clare Stewart, who stepped down in September.

Kuyper will join IFFR in mid-January 2027 and work alongside Stewart during a handover period through to the conclusion of the 2027 edition of the festival, which runs from 28 January to 7 February.

Kuyper is currently Managing Director of Amerpodia, which operates three cultural institutions in Amsterdam: Rode Hoed, Felix Meritis and De Nieuwe Liefde. He also previously served as Business Director at the Netherlands Film Festival, and before that as Managing Director of LUX in Nijmegen and LantarenVenster in Rotterdam. At LantarenVenster, a longstanding IFFR venue, he helped establish year-round collaborations with the festival. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Rotterdam Unveils First Titles Locked To World Premiere At 2027 Edition News Cate Blanchett's Displacement Film Fund To Support Short Films By Mo Amer, Annemarie Jacir, Rithy Panh, Akuol de Mabior & Bao Nguyen

