&#x201C;I&#x2019;ve particularly appreciated his clear judgment and the openness and enthusiasm he brings to our conversations about the festival&#x2019;s future,&#x201D; Kaludjercic added. &#x201C;I&#x2019;m looking forward to working alongside him and the team, building on what we have developed together and continuing to create opportunities for filmmakers and audiences.&#x201D;

Kuyper added: &#x201C;I am very much looking forward to working with Vanja and the team to build on the achievements of this internationally leading festival, firmly rooted in Rotterdam and closely connected to the film sector. With my entrepreneurial spirit, I want to help secure a strong future for IFFR in which its artistic ambitions can flourish.&#x201D;

The Geico Gecko has, over decades, become a Madison Avenue phenom. Can it also develop into a holiday tradition?

The creature doesn&#x2019;t have antlers, hooves or a shiny nose — and therefore looks nothing like Rudolph, the Red-Nosed Reindeer. If a big bet by the insurance giant pays off later this week, however, the famous ad character may, like the legendary Christmas figure, be part of holiday tidings for years to come. Related Stories 'You Can See Everything' Becomes Rare Documentary to Surpass $100 Million Globally 'You Can See Everything' Has Biggest Opening Weekend for Doc in U.K. Box Office History

Geico will on Thursday debut a two-minute-long vignette during NBC&#x2019;s telecast of the Macy's Thanksgiving Day parade that shows a host of its popular ad characters trying to boost Christmas spirit by 15%, after hearing what they believe is a message from Santa (the plotline plays off Geico&#x2019;s famous offer of helping consumers save 15% on their car insurance, a message the company hopes will resonate with consumers worried about rising prices). All the characters are handcrafted puppets that move via stop-motion animation, and the ad looks a lot like a vintage holiday special along the lines of 1964&#x2019;s &#x201C; Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer &#x201D; or 1974&#x2019;s &#x201C;The Year Without a Santa Claus.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In an era when consumers are more eager than ever to avoid traditional commercials, advertisers have entered &#x201C;a war for attention,&#x201D; says Ariana Orpello, Geico&#x2019;s chief marketing officer , during a recent interview. Insurance ads, filled with clever characters and snappy slogans , can be quite popular, she says, but research suggests that consumers are inundated with pitches from players including Geico, Progressive, Allstate, Liberty Mutual and State Farm, among others. &#x201C;I think we have a responsibility to make sure we are clear in our message and that we are respectful of the attention we are trying to earn,&#x201D; she says. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Other advertisers have tried to seize attention during Macy&#x2019;s annual holiday extravaganza. In 2019, Comcast surprised viewers during an NBC telecast of the Macy&#x2019;s Thanksgiving Day Parade with a vignette showing E.T., the alien protagonist from the blockbuster 1982 film of the same name, meeting up with an older Elliott, played by Henry Thomas, the actor who also inhabited the role as a child.

Yet the pressure on traditional commercials to capture interest has grown exponentially more intense. More ads have focused on getting viewers to make a quick purchase by clicking with their remotes to trigger an on-screen prompt, or on getting audiences to use a displayed QR code to get more information. Ads that burnish an overall brand or stick in the memory for a longer period of time have become more difficult to create.

As a result, more advertisers are trying to create stand-alone content, rather than good ol&#x2019; commercials. Taco Bell, the Yum Brands fast-food chain, recently debuted its own golf tournament that streamed on Peacock and aired on Golf Channel. Some, like Pepsi, have tested running game shows that they produce and show via a media outlet, like Fox. Others, like Under Armour, are launching their own internal studios so as to be in a better position to produce and distribute timely content.

&#x201C;If you see the same thing over and over again, you're just going to get annoyed,&#x201D; says Orpello. &#x201C;Hopefully you don't get as tired of things like this because they actually make you feel something different. &#x2029;We are not just trying to sell you something but also provide you something that you didn't even know you wanted at that moment.&#x201D;

Geico has tried in the past to break free of traditional advertising. In 2024, Geico unveiled a 15-minute documentary on the Gecko&#x2019;s fictional origins and childhood. TV fans may recall that Geico&#x2019;s popular Cavemen commercial characters were the center of an ABC sitcom in 2007, developed in part by some of the people who worked on the original ads. The show did not generate much positive reaction and was quickly canceled.

Geico&#x2019;s holiday gambit is not cheap or easy. NBC has in many cases been seeking more than $1 million for 30 seconds of ad time in this year&#x2019;s Macy&#x2019;s parade, according to Guideline, a tracker of ad spending. Adding to the tensions: Geico came up with the concept just over three months ago, creating a scramble by its longtime adverting partner, The Martin Agency, as well as two production studios, Passion Pictures and Screen Novelties, to get it all done in time. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s a very labor-intensive process,&#x201D; says Justin Booth-Clibborn, an executive producer who was intimately involved in the process. Twelve different puppets were made by hand, using materials such as rope to craft the hair of the Geico Caveman, or a sock with festive designs to create another character&#x2019;s holiday sweater. A crew of about 80 people was hired to make all the elements come together. Every second of footage represents &#x201C;12 frames we are animating,&#x201D; says Booth-Clibborn. &#x201C;In every frame, you have to move a little piece of the arm or the face or the hand or the leg, and then you take a shot and do the next frame. You have about two to three seconds of animation per day.&#x201D;

Big-budget films have &#x201C;dailies,&#x201D; or once-a-day check-ins to examine work in progress. Agencies working for Geico had &#x201C;hourlies,&#x201D; says Jerry Hoak, chief creative officer of The Martin Agency, part of Omnicom Group, where personnel have worked on Geico campaigns for decades. &#x201C;The thing with stop motion, you can&#x2019;t just reshoot it. You know, one shot takes the whole day,&#x201D; he says. The production team would send regular pictures &#x201C;Are you ok with this frame? We are moving. And we and the client all just held hands,&#x201D; he recounted.

Greater worries were at play, too. Will characters like the Gecko the Geico Caveman, Caleb the &#x201C;Hump Day&#x201D; Camel and Maxwell the Pig translate to animation? &#x201C;Especially for the Gecko, it&#x2019;s like, how do we make sure we don&#x2019;t ruin this icon?&#x201D; asks Hoak. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s as important to Geico as Mickey Mouse is to Disney. You have to do him right.&#x201D;

One edge Geico has over other advertisers is years of ad history, with dozens of characters, slogans and scenes that have caught hold in the nation&#x2019;s collective consciousness. Look for at least 15 &#x201C;Easter eggs&#x201D; to surface during the commercial, says Hoak, that nod to some of them. Viewers who pause the spot when a newspaper pops up will find several articles they might start reading. &#x201C;The idea is the more you hunt, the more you find,&#x201D; the ad executive says. &#x201C;There have been so many commercials that people love.&#x201D;

Geico is working to make sure people see the new work. A teaser will appear Wednesday evening alerting consumers to the vignette in the parade. The company has hired Devo to appear on a float during the Thanksgiving parade, and the ad is expected to follow soon afterwards. And the two-minute-long work will also appear in movie theaters as part of cinema ad buys. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The hope is that the Geico special will resonate with consumers as much as the Hershey&#x2019;s holiday ad featuring the company&#x2019;s chocolate kisses being used as bells to sound out a Christmas carol, or the toy trucks sold by the Hess energy company around Yuletide.

Indeed, Geico shot additional footage that might allow for new editions of the spot, or future pieces of content around different holidays. &#x201C;There might be some there might be some stuff in the future that will surprise people,&#x201D; says Hoak. &#x201C;We would love this thing to expand. There's no reason why we couldn't do it for Halloween or, you know, other moments throughout the year and create specials.&#x201D;

Does Geico have the makings of &#x201C;A Charlie Brown Christmas&#x201D; on its hands? &#x201C;That&#x2019;s the dream,&#x201D; says Orpello.

Factual prod-co group Passion, behind documentaries including the BAFTA-winning &#x201C;Super/Man: The Christopher Reeve Story,&#x201D; is restructuring its executive leadership team as it eyes a new phase of growth.

CEO Nick Southgate, who has led the company for five years, is moving to an executive co-chair role alongside founder and executive chair Andrew Ruhemann. He will be replaced by David Moulton. Related Stories Chase Infiniti Coming-of-Age Drama 'The Julia Set' Sells Out for HanWay (EXCLUSIVE) 'The Witcher' Star Freya Allan to Lead Joachim Rønning’s Horror Movie 'System' (EXCLUSIVE)

Moulton will be joined by Hamish Fergusson as chief creative officer and Georgina Mantle as managing director. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Passion, which is comprised of Passion Docs, Passion Planety and KEO Films, will focus on sustaining international growth in a new television era. Moulton will oversee the company as it scales high-end documentary and unscripted original output as well as expanding returnable formats, long-term IP and digital programming.

&#x201C;Audiences are discovering and experiencing stories in new ways, and Passion is determined to lead that shift,&#x201D; said Moulton. &#x201C;I&#x2019;m delighted to welcome Georgina and Hamish into their new roles, as their vision will help us embrace digital innovation across every part of the business. By pairing our extraordinary creative legacy with new technology, platforms and data-driven thinking, we will unlock fresh growth across all our labels and reach audiences worldwide in bolder ways. The momentum we&#x2019;re seeing is incredible, and I can&#x2019;t wait to see what we build together.&#x201D;

Southgate added: &#x201C;Over the last five years we have built Passion into a documentary powerhouse, now is the right time for David and his exceptional team to take the company on its new journey to capitalise on the growing global demand for high-end unscripted programming. We couldn&#x2019;t be more confident in this team&#x2019;s vision for the future.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Mantle, who will report to Moulton, will be tasked with leading the group&#x2019;s strategic growth, including its genre footprint and IP development, building international co-pros and steering digital strategy. She was previously global creative director at ITN Productions, where she oversaw development, played a key role in strategy and helped build the brand&#x2019;s expanded digital division.

Fergusson has spent three years as Passion&#x2019;s creative director, leading the group&#x2019;s creative strategy and shaping its development slates as well as individual leadership across the labels.

Passion is known for projects such as &#x201C;McCartney: The Hunt for the Lost Bass&#x201D; and last week announced a new landmark Bruce Springstee doc, &#x201C;When The Walls Came Down&#x201D; in partnership with Legendary Entertainment and Sony Music. Other recently-unveiled projects include &#x201C;Hantavirus: The Inside Story&#x201D; for NatGeo alongside Muck Media.

EXCLUSIVE: Ties That Bind , the training and co-production program for European and Asian producers, is returning to Busan in South Korea through a partnership with Asian Contents & Film Market ( ACFM ), Korean Film Council ( KOFIC ) and Japan&#x2019;s Visual Industry Promotion Organization ( VIPO ).

In 2027, the first of two Ties That Bind workshops will take place April 25-29, 2027, in Udine, Italy, as part of Udine Far East Film Festival (FEFF) and Focus Asia, as it has done for several years.

The second workshop will take place in early October 2027 in Busan, South Korea, as part of the Busan International Film Festival and ACFM. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Justin H. Min Starrer 'Journey There' & Hong Sangsoo's 'Nowhere To Lay My Eyes' Sell To Multiple Territories News 'A Chronicle Of Minor Things' & 'Goldfish' Among Award Winners At Busan's Asian Project Market

